winemac: HADRON_MAC_BACKGROUND=1 keeps the program off the screen.

For automated runs (a test or a script driving a game) on a Mac someone is using at the same time.
The program never activates itself or unhides, and LaunchServices is told not to activate it either
(compat_run.sh launches with open -g). Its windows go to the lowest window level, under the desktop
picture: nothing of them shows, yet they stay on screen, so they keep drawing and a capture by window id
(screencapture -l) still works. They ignore the mouse, and the program never warps, clips or reads the
host cursor (GetCursorPos keeps wineserver's position) or changes a display mode. Input comes only from
inside Wine, as SendHardwareInput (host-style hardware input to Wine's foreground window), and goes
without the macOS input method: an input method the user selected would take keys from a program that
is never the active app and give nothing back.

Unset or 0: no change.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
